<title>CHILE: Banco Santiago Q1 net at 8.3 billion pesos.</title>
<headline>Banco Santiago Q1 net at 8.3 billion pesos.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco Santiago reported first-quarter profits of 8.29 billion pesos, the Banking Superintendency said.</p>
<p>No comparative figures were possible because the bank was formed in January this year with the merger of Banco de Santiago and Banco O'Higgins. But the new figures gave a snapshot of the bank's financial situation.</p>
<p>Outstanding loans were 3.27 trillion pesos, capital reserves were 273 billion, and its annualized return on capital and reserves was 19.7 percent, said the superintendency.</p>
<p>((--Roger Atwood, Santiago newsroom +56-2-699-5595 x211))</p>
